    <Placemark>
      <description>I warmly welcome you in this &quot;story-telling&quot; old house, where, at the beginning of the century the hard-working and hospitable Kéhli family opened its small restaurant, and ran it with such a care, that mother Kéhli&apos;s name became famous alredy in her life. The former &quot;Old-Buda&quot; with its rickety houses, workshops, stores, little pubs inviting bohemians, artists, students disappeared more than twenty-five years ago. Citizens of swabian and jewish origin used to live here together with their Hungarian neighbours in mutual appreciation.

The Restaurant Kéhli, sorrunded by some similary old houses keeps a little island of the past arnong the monotonous rows of cubical houses. Thanks to the former well-known regular guest, Gyula Krúdy, the great Hungarian writer, it survived the annihilation and it is still open.

The poet of fragnances, tastes colours and of the fairs laides lulls and enchantes you among these walls. It reminds you of the athmosphere of simple human joys - the absolving power of everyday celebration of friendship and love, and it is very joyful to be a part of this at the end of our century.

Dear Guests! I ask you to visit our house often, and bring with yourselves everyone who, apart from the joy of food - the benefit of the Hungarian citizens&apos; cuisin and the wine cellars - wishes to enjoy dance and music - through the good and bad spirits of their souls on the music of violin and accordian.</description>
      <name>Kéhli Vendéglő</name>
      <View>
        <longitude>19.04402972922406</longitude>
        <latitude>47.53713167387211</latitude>
        <range>646.4000262321874</range>
