    <Placemark>
      <description>I. Batthyány tér 7

The Angelika Cukrászda is housed in a historic building next to St. Anne&apos;s Church on Buda&apos;s Batthyány tér. The sunken rooms of this cavernous cafe provide the perfect retreat on a hot summer day. The place was recently extended to include a grill restaurant outside and a complex of terraces on three levels. Now you will find a perfect view of the Parliament building and the Chain Bridge. The stained-glass windows and marble floors contrast beautifully with the off-white canvas upholstery and cast-iron furniture. You can choose from among a selection of excellent pastries, coffees, and teas (a rarity in Budapest, a city of serious coffee addicts). There is a small gallery inside the coffeehouse, where artworks are displayed.</description>
      <name>Angelika Cukrászda</name>
