    <Placemark>
      <description>Set amidst the tranquil surroundings of the Városliget (City Park), the Széchenyi Baths is a grand old building to which Budapest families flock during the summer. The unisex outdoor pool has a extremely convivial atmosphere - old timers play chess on floating boards while everyone else just lazes around. The Széchenyi&apos;s Turkish baths are housed away from the main pool, while outside there&apos;s a statue of Zsigmond Vilmos who discovered the thermal springs here.</description>
      <name>Szechenyi Spa Baths</name>
      <View>
        <longitude>19.08260066688371</longitude>
        <latitude>47.5186521968574</latitude>
        <range>350.5995685674523</range>
        <tilt>-1.436308438036073e-010</tilt>
        <heading>0.01554155407057936</heading>
      </View>
      <visibility>0</visibility>
      <styleUrl>root://styleMaps#default?iconId=0x307</styleUrl>
      <Style>
