    <Placemark>
      <description>Laser Theater 19:30 Monday 29/11
J.M. Jarre

Cobwebs woven of emerald laser light are into transparent veils by ruby flashes of light where plusating polygons dance madly amid thousands of vivid lightwaves. suddenly, a fireless fireworks explodes in the midst of a cavaroting vortex of light to crown this enrapturing celebration. This is the birt of light- music. 

Oxigene, Magnetic Fields and Equinoxe have given birt to the Jarre universe. Zoolook, a joint production with Laurie Anderson, sort of populate this planet. The LaserTheater gives you is own interpretation of the Jarre message. The show uses is special, exclusively laser-brush, drawing to inhabit the starlit cupola of the Planetarium. 

This visit to the realm of breathtaking lights will endow the visitor with the feeling strolling through a diferent dimension of the universe.</description>
      <name>Planetarium</name>
