    <Placemark>
      <description>Budapest Christmas Fair
(Vörösmarty square) 
         Programme selection             
 Cultural life 
 Important programmes and festivals during the year 
 Calendar packed with programmes 
 Ticket Offices 
 Sightseeing programmes 
 

Description:


The traditional Budapest Christmas Fair is the greatest event during the weeks of advent which provides a special holiday atmosphere to the heart of the city. 
Visiting this event on one of Budapest’s most beautiful squares, the Vörösmarty square, can be an excellent programme -not only for residents, but the foreign tourists as well-, since the event offers a variety of interesting programmes, including a special fair with products and gifts made of natural raw materials with traditional handicraft techniques, the Advent Calendar, exhibitions and other cultural and musik programmes. Performers from all over Hungary are showing traditional folk dances, folk music and songs. It is a good opportunity to learn a little more about the people and customs of Hungary. There are over 100 wooden stands, festively decorated and offering specialities, crafts, paintings, glass manufacturing, holiday dishes. Only unique products of natural ingredients are sold on the fair, and the quality of goods is controlled by the jury of the Association of Hungarian Folk Arts. The spirit of Christmas is ensured by stage plays, musicians and dancers. Children can enjoy the live Bethlehem games, the dancehouse- and handcraft programmes, others can try the typical Hungarian Christmas cuisine offering a wide range of pancakes, sausages and glowing wine. The Gerbeaud Advent Calendar is the highlight of these days since the facade of the most beautiful patisserie, the Gerbeaud-House is transformed into an advent calendar, and pictures of 24 contemporary artists will be exhibited in the windows. The opening ceremony of a new window, along with a light and sound show, starts each day, at 5 pm. The fair is held from november 26th till december 24th 2004. Opening hours: 10am till 7pm every day.</description>
      <name>Vörösmarty Ter (pedestrian)</name>
      <View>
        <longitude>19.05075622321657</longitude>
        <latitude>47.49633273797814</latitude>
